package itest

/*
Real DNS traffic, captured from a public resolver and frozen here.

The mock upstream replays these responses byte for byte, so the tests check that
elodin passes genuine wire data through unharmed - including name compression,
DNSSEC records and record types the codec does not model natively. Generating
the fixtures with our own encoder instead would let a codec bug agree with
itself and still pass.

Each entry stores the exact query that produced the response, so tests can send
that query and have the question sections line up.
*/

